WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.832
A loop replays forever, so there is no real start or end.

2
00:00:02.832 --> 00:00:08.000
The last moment has to flow straight into the first one, like the dot going all the way around a circle.

3
00:00:08.000 --> 00:00:10.373
The seam is the moment where the end meets the start.

4
00:00:10.373 --> 00:00:13.687
On the left the ball ends in a different place than it began, so it jumps.

5
00:00:13.687 --> 00:00:17.000
On the right it ends exactly where it started, so you cannot see the join.

6
00:00:17.000 --> 00:00:21.919
The easiest fix is to copy the very first keyframe and paste it at the end of the timeline.

7
00:00:21.919 --> 00:00:25.000
Same values at both ends means the loop closes perfectly.

8
00:00:25.000 --> 00:00:29.507
For text, let the old word begin leaving while the new word is already arriving.

9
00:00:29.507 --> 00:00:33.000
That overlap hides the handover, so your eye never sees a gap.
